<title>GREECE: Most Greek closed-end funds trade at discount in Q1.</title>
<headline>Most Greek closed-end funds trade at discount in Q1.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's 16 closed-end investment funds listed on the Athens stock exchange had a market capitalisation of 143.6 billion drachmas at the end of the first quarter, the Association of Institutional Investors said.</p>
<p>Launching a monthly review, the association provided statistics showing 11 out the 16 funds were trading at a discount to their net asset value (NAV) at the end of first quarter.</p>
<p>Only four funds -- Ergo, Alpha, Hellenic Invest and National --  managed to outperform the market's 43.4 percent gain in the first quarter.</p>
<p>    FUND			MKT CAP*    RETURN**  PREMIUM/DISCOUNT</p>
<p>				 (drs bln)		     (to NAV)</p>
<p>Alpha Invest	  46.1	  43.5%	     8.7%</p>
<p>Hellenic Invest     31.9	  63.9%	    12.3%</p>
<p>Progress		16.4	  26.7%	   -17.9%</p>
<p>Ergo Invest	   15.5	  62.8%	   -16.0%</p>
<p>National Invest     12.9	  52.5%	    13.6%</p>
<p>Piraeus Invest	 4.4	  42.4%	    -1.4%</p>
<p>Ionian Invest	  3.4	  33.5%	    11.0%</p>
<p>Development Fund     2.2	  37.5%	   -20.7%</p>
<p>Aeolian		  2.1	  38.9%	   -19.3%</p>
<p>Commercial	     1.8	  24.3%	    10.7%</p>
<p>Dias		     1.4	   3.4%	   -17.7%</p>
<p>Orion		    1.3	  26.8%	   -18.9%</p>
<p>Interinvest	    1.0	  11.1%	   -18.5%</p>
<p>Exelixi		  1.0	  39.0%	   -20.3%</p>
<p>Aspis		    0.9	 -11.0%	   -15.4%</p>
<p>Mediterranean	  0.5	  18.1%	   -24.2%</p>
<p>TOTAL			    143.6</p>
<p>* market cap and premium/discount to NAV based on closing</p>
<p>prices at the end of first quarter</p>
<p>** return since the beginning of the year</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
